ir has climbed from the 160.60 area in early July and has spent the past week establishing itself above the 163.00 handle, a level that had previously acted as a ceiling during mid-month ranging.\n\nThe structure story over the past month is one of grinding, methodical dollar strength. After a sharp sell-off on 2 July that briefly dragged price to 160.68 \u2014 a zone that has now registered four prior reactions and sits as the most significant structural support on the board \u2014 buyers reasserted themselves with conviction. The recovery was not impulsive; it was a slow, coiling advance through the 161.30\u2013162.50 band before a decisive break higher on 21 July opened the door to the 163\u2013164 region. That July low around 160.60 now represents the level that would fundamentally challenge the bullish read. Below it, the 159.87 and 159.64 prior reaction zones come into view, with 159.44 \u2014 the most frequently tested support on the chart at five touches \u2014 offering the deeper structural floor.\n\nOn the H1 timeframe, the picture is one of short-term digestion following Friday's spike high. Price pushed to 164.09 in the 21:00 UTC candle before reversing sharply, and the subsequent overnight and morning price action has been a gradual drift lower, with the 163.46\u2013163.50 area providing a tentative intraday floor across the 11:00\u201312:00 UTC candles. The current 163.57 print sits in the middle of a relatively tight range, with sellers appearing to cap rallies toward 163.70\u2013163.75 and buyers stepping in around 163.46. A clean hourly close back above 163.85 would suggest the drift lower is corrective rather than the start of something more meaningful.\n\nToday's calendar is light on high-impact USD events. Durable Goods Orders and the Core reading are both flagged as low impact at 08:30 UTC, meaning they are unlikely to generate sustained directional momentum on their own. That said, any meaningful miss or beat relative to expectations could produce a brief volatility spike in an otherwise quiet session, and with price sitting in a compressed intraday range, the reaction to even second-tier data deserves attention.\n\nThe bullish read holds while price maintains itself above the 162.80\u2013163.00 region \u2014 the prior breakout area from late July. A sustained daily close beneath 162.00 would begin to erode confidence in the current leg, and a return to 160.60 would represent a material structural challenge to the broader trend. To the upside, the 164.00\u2013164.10 area is the immediate ceiling to watch.\n\nThis is editorial analysis, not financial advice. Trading involves substantial risk of loss.", "sample": false}